# Swift
.build/
.swiftpm/
# `!*.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` alone does NOT work: a plain `*.xcodeproj` pattern makes git
# ignore the whole directory and never descend into it at all, so a negation for a path inside it
# has no effect — confirmed with `git check-ignore -v`, not assumed. Ignoring the *contents*
# instead (`*.xcodeproj/*`) keeps git descending into the bundle, so the negations below actually
# track the two files a checkout needs (the project definition and the workspace it wraps) while
# everything else in the bundle (user-specific state) stays ignored, both directly here and via
# the standalone `xcuserdata/` rule below, which still matches at any depth.
*.xcodeproj/*
!*.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
!*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace
!*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/contents.xcworkspacedata
!*.xcodeproj/xcshareddata
!*.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/**
DerivedData/
.DS_Store

## Xcode user settings
xcuserdata/

